# The image builds Insights from the remote fork named in docker/apps.json, so
# nothing from this working tree reaches the image except the three files
# re-included below.
#
# Deny-all first. That is what structurally keeps .git/config -- which currently
# holds a plaintext GitHub PAT (docs/mcp-IMPLEMENTATION.md 8 I) -- out of the
# build context, no matter how the Dockerfile is edited later. It also cuts the
# context from ~1 GB (frontend/node_modules is 411 MB, insights/public/frontend
# is 28 MB, plus .git) down to a few KB.
#
# WARNING: if you ever add `COPY . .` to the Dockerfile it will copy nothing.
# Add explicit `!` re-includes for whatever that step needs, and think hard
# before re-including .git.
*

!docker/apps.json
!docker/resources/nginx-template.conf
!docker/resources/nginx-entrypoint.sh
